  "prefLabel": "En 502.03 Cubic foot",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 502.03 \"Cubic foot\" means, for the purpose of measurement of gas to a customer, the amount of gas which occupies a volume of one cubic foot under the conditions existing in the customer's meter as and where installed, provided such meter is not subject to abnormal temperature conditions unless the meter is designed with temperature compensation.\n\nSource. #13796, eff 10-25-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en500.html"
